<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
<p class="font-bold">The one kilogram of dry matter never changes.</p>
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 212" class="w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="potato-title potato-desc">
<title id="potato-title">One hundred kilograms of potatoes drying to fifty kilograms</title><desc id="potato-desc">Before drying: 99 kilograms water and 1 kilogram dry matter. After drying: 49 kilograms water and the same 1 kilogram dry matter. The total halves to 50 kilograms.</desc>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="18"><text x="15" y="26">Before: 100 kg</text><text x="15" y="123">After: 50 kg</text></g>
<rect x="15" y="40" width="396" height="42" fill="#387a91"/><rect x="411" y="40" width="4" height="42" fill="#bd4b37"/>
<rect x="15" y="138" width="196" height="42" fill="#387a91"/><rect x="211" y="138" width="4" height="42" fill="#bd4b37"/>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="17"><text x="18" y="104">99 kg water + 1 kg dry</text><text x="18" y="201">49 kg water + 1 kg dry</text></g>
</svg>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">The dry portion is fixed at 1 kg. Initially that is 1% of 100 kg. Once it is 2% of the total, the total must be 1 ÷ 0.02 = <strong>50 kg</strong>. The thin red end cap is the same 1 kg in both bars, drawn to scale.</figcaption></figure>